   "source": [
    "# Lab 3: NumPy + Pandas for Eye-Tracking Data\n",
    "\n",
    "### Goal:\n",
    "In this lab, you will learn the basic Python tools used for eye-tracking data analysis:\n",
    " - NumPy (for numerical calculations)\n",
    " - Pandas (for working with CSV files and tables)\n",
    " - Matplotlib (for simple visualization)\n",
    "\n",
    " These tools will be used in the next labs for\n",
    " calibration analysis and gaze interaction.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Task 1 — NumPy Arrays\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective:\n",
    " Understand how gaze data can be stored as numerical arrays.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Instructions:\n",
    "1. Create two NumPy arrays:\n",
    "       - gaze_x\n",
    "       - gaze_y\n",
    "2. Print both arrays\n",
    "\n",
    "### Observe:\n",
    " - Why is gaze data stored as many values instead of one?\n",
    " - What does each value represent?\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ed6cd1d3-51c4-4fe7-9a46-804e5b3836e4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "gaze_x = np.array([400, 405, 398, 410, 402])\n",
    "gaze_y = np.array([300, 298, 305, 310, 299])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Gaze X:\", gaze_x)\n",
    "print(\"Gaze Y:\", gaze_y)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "150a638c-65af-4930-92b9-203541d38ff2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 2 — Basic Statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective:\n",
    "Calculate simple statistics from gaze data.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Instructions:\n",
    "1. Calculate:\n",
    "       - mean\n",
    "       - standard deviation\n",
    "2. Print the results\n",
    "\n",
    "### Observe:\n",
    " - What does the mean represent?\n",
    " - What does a high standard deviation mean?\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b6b8000f-e58c-435e-b303-40b3dfe735d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Mean X:\", np.mean(gaze_x))\n",
    "print(\"Mean Y:\", np.mean(gaze_y))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Std X:\", np.std(gaze_x))\n",
    "print(\"Std Y:\", np.std(gaze_y))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "15403cea-6cdd-4a86-9dcc-2dec896c8c3f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 3 — Distance from the Target\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective:\n",
    " Measure how far gaze is from the true target.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Instructions:\n",
    " Assume the true target is located at:\n",
    "       TargetX = 400\n",
    "       TargetY = 300\n",
    "\n",
    " 1. Calculate the distance (error) for each gaze point\n",
    " 2. Print the error values\n",
    " 3. Calculate the mean error\n",
    "\n",
    "### Observe:\n",
    " - Which gaze points are most accurate?\n",
    " - Which are farthest from the target?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6f112930-e3f5-44f7-96f2-94de6f046098",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "target_x = 400\n",
    "target_y = 300\n",
    "\n",
    "error = np.sqrt(\n",
    "    (gaze_x - target_x) ** 2 +\n",
    "    (gaze_y - target_y) ** 2\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Error values:\", error)\n",
    "print(\"Mean Error:\", np.mean(error))\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7879f6c7-c0fb-4863-97f2-912629044e73",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 4 — Create a Pandas DataFrame\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective:\n",
    "Store gaze data in a table format.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Instructions:\n",
    "1. Create a DataFrame with:\n",
    "       - GazeX\n",
    "       - GazeY\n",
    "       - Error\n",
    "2. Display the table\n",
    "\n",
    "### Observe:\n",
    " - Why is a table useful for eye-tracking analysis?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a902ff93-187d-4475-a289-1a6c0c66f80c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"GazeX\": gaze_x,\n",
    "    \"GazeY\": gaze_y,\n",
    "    \"Error\": error\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "48f232e1-9849-4831-a695-ec0c889e698d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
